1
00:00:54,421 --> 00:00:56,421
The film you are about to see...

2
00:00:56,521 --> 00:00:59,621
...is based on the tragedy suffered by a group
of young people.

3
00:01:02,121 --> 00:01:04,926
And it is all the more tragic because they were
so young.

4
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:07,771
But even if they had lived longer...

5
00:01:07,871 --> 00:01:11,447
...they could never have expected or wished to
witness...

6
00:01:11,786 --> 00:01:15,305
...the madness and macabre horrors they saw that
day.

7
00:01:16,313 --> 00:01:18,771
For them, an idyllic summer afternoon...

8
00:01:18,821 --> 00:01:20,061
...turned into a nightmare.

9
00:01:21,971 --> 00:01:26,103
For thirty years, the records lay forgotten...

10
00:01:26,390 --> 00:01:28,471
...in the Travis County Police Department.

11
00:01:31,956 --> 00:01:36,521
More than 1,300 pieces of evidence were
collected from the crime scene...

12
00:01:36,571 --> 00:01:38,071
...at the Hewitt residence.

13
00:01:41,871 --> 00:01:46,121
"House of Horror Shocks Nation"
"Texas Massacre"

14
00:01:46,261 --> 00:01:49,171
But no piece of evidence was more compelling...

15
00:01:49,371 --> 00:01:51,592
...than the confidential police footage...

16
00:01:51,790 --> 00:01:53,733
...of the crime-scene investigation.

17
00:01:54,664 --> 00:01:55,900
Testing.

18
00:01:56,976 --> 00:01:58,421
All right.

19
00:01:58,571 --> 00:02:03,269
Today is August 20, 1973. The time is 3:47 p.m.

20
00:02:03,553 --> 00:02:06,071
We're at the Hewitt residence...

21
00:02:06,171 --> 00:02:07,721
...room 17...

22
00:02:07,821 --> 00:02:09,671
...where the first victim was found.

23
00:02:10,470 --> 00:02:12,121
We're going to conduct an investigation.

24
00:02:12,221 --> 00:02:15,355
We're going down the stairs to the crime scene.

25
00:02:18,135 --> 00:02:19,471
Here.

26
00:02:19,571 --> 00:02:22,866
These are fingernail marks on the wall. There
are more over here.

27
00:02:25,237 --> 00:02:27,240
And there's something here. It looks like...

28
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:28,921
...it appears to be...

29
00:02:29,893 --> 00:02:33,485
...hair and broken fingernails.

30
00:02:34,972 --> 00:02:38,093
Well, now we're going to enter the crime scene.

31
00:02:38,471 --> 00:02:39,771
The events of that day...

32
00:02:39,821 --> 00:02:43,854
...became part of one of the most bizarre crimes
in U.S. history.

33
00:02:44,521 --> 00:02:47,071
"The Texas Chainsaw Massacre."

34
00:02:50,321 --> 00:02:53,571
Don't let go! Not yet!

35
00:02:53,671 --> 00:02:54,871
Now!

36
00:02:58,421 --> 00:03:01,171
August 18, 1973.

37
00:03:17,421 --> 00:03:18,953
Could somebody make him stop singing?

38
00:03:23,441 --> 00:03:25,871
- I think you have a beautiful voice, honey.
- Thank you!

39
00:03:38,811 --> 00:03:40,705
Didn't you hear what I told you yesterday?

40
00:03:44,432 --> 00:03:45,771
You're amazing.

41
00:03:49,178 --> 00:03:50,421
Could you two knock it off for a minute?

42
00:03:51,021 --> 00:03:52,321
Hello?

43
00:03:52,421 --> 00:03:53,671
Hello?

44
00:03:53,821 --> 00:03:56,271
Could you take a break? Just for a minute?

45
00:03:56,901 --> 00:03:59,271
Thirty-three thousand Americans a day...

46
00:03:59,371 --> 00:04:01,221
...are infected with sexually transmitted
diseases...

47
