If you're trying to scare me, I'm getting out of
here.

261
00:21:15,486 --> 00:21:16,989
- Erin, come on.
- Let me go.

262
00:21:17,921 --> 00:21:19,621
Erin, come on. Cut the crap.

263
00:21:47,878 --> 00:21:49,182
- Kemper!
- Erin!

264
00:21:51,270 --> 00:21:52,171
Erin!

265
00:21:53,822 --> 00:21:55,171
Erin, where are you?

266
00:21:59,527 --> 00:22:00,921
What's in there?

267
00:22:06,254 --> 00:22:07,597
- It's okay.
- Go on.

268
00:22:13,802 --> 00:22:15,232
- I've got it.
- All right.

269
00:22:25,551 --> 00:22:27,249
Oh, God! Oh, God!

270
00:22:28,255 --> 00:22:29,321
Damn it!

271
00:22:30,671 --> 00:22:32,421
Give me something to jam the door.

272
00:22:32,771 --> 00:22:35,901
- You asshole! You're such an asshole!
- Did you see that...?

273
00:22:39,966 --> 00:22:41,167
I didn't do that.

274
00:22:49,768 --> 00:22:53,221
If somebody's in there, cut it out, okay?

275
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:55,777
I'm serious! Just come out!

276
00:23:08,369 --> 00:23:09,291
Who are you?

277
00:23:14,299 --> 00:23:15,871
What did you do to her?

278
00:23:17,205 --> 00:23:17,948
What?

279
00:23:19,601 --> 00:23:22,174
The girl out there. In the van.

280
00:23:23,542 --> 00:23:25,221
We didn't do anything to her.

281
00:23:25,574 --> 00:23:27,271
She did it herself.

282
00:23:35,519 --> 00:23:36,217
Oh, my God.

283
00:23:40,479 --> 00:23:42,271
Promise you won't hurt me?

284
00:23:49,621 --> 00:23:50,997
Hey, did you do this?

285
00:24:04,921 --> 00:24:06,121
Hey, buddy...

286
00:24:08,171 --> 00:24:10,271
This is the old Crawford mill, right?

287
00:24:13,533 --> 00:24:14,971
My name's Erin.

288
00:24:16,638 --> 00:24:17,971
Jedidiah.

289
00:24:23,909 --> 00:24:25,221
Hey, little guy.

290
00:24:25,396 --> 00:24:28,396
We're waiting for the sheriff. Do you know where
he is?

291
00:24:30,561 --> 00:24:31,981
All right, where?

292
00:24:33,663 --> 00:24:36,321
At home. Getting drunk.

293
00:24:36,521 --> 00:24:38,171
Brilliant. Let's go.

294
00:24:38,471 --> 00:24:40,271
If the sheriff doesn't care...

295
00:24:40,321 --> 00:24:41,971
...why should we?

296
00:24:42,901 --> 00:24:44,221
Does he live around here?

297
00:24:47,080 --> 00:24:49,573
You know, we had tickets to a big concert.

298
00:24:50,633 --> 00:24:52,371
Can we drive there?

299
00:24:53,234 --> 00:24:54,671
The road doesn't go all the way.

300
00:24:54,721 --> 00:24:56,221
You can only get there on foot.

301
00:24:56,696 --> 00:24:59,951
I think we should leave now. I mean, right now.

302
00:25:01,721 --> 00:25:03,121
How do I get to his house?

303
00:25:39,947 --> 00:25:41,330
Hey, little mutant.

304
00:25:45,519 --> 00:25:46,621
Come on, give me that.

305
00:25:46,671 --> 00:25:48,921
Get out of here. That's police evidence.

306
00:26:26,225 --> 00:26:27,621
Anybody home?

307
00:26:29,580 --> 00:26:31,671
- Hello?
- What do you want?

308
00:26:32,706 --> 00:26:36,200
- Are you the sheriff?
- Do I look like a sheriff?

309
00:26:37,265 --> 00:26:40,121
- I don't know, I can't see you.
- Step away from the door.

310
00:26:49,960 --> 00:26:51,397
The sheriff doesn't live here.

311
00:26:52,508 --> 00:26:54,521
You can call him if you want.

312
00:26:54,721 --> 00:26:56,712
Thanks, we'd like to.

313
00:26:59,621 --> 00:27:03,345
Wipe your feet before coming inside.

314
00:27:09,521 --> 00:27:12,271
I said she could call. You wait outside.

315
00:27:12,321 --> 00:27:13,571
All right, boss.

316
00:27:14,134 --> 00:27:16,444
- I don't want any trouble.
- Don't shoot.

317
00:27:22,731 --> 00:27:23,684
Allow me.

318
00:27:42,021 --> 00:27:43,271
I'll dial for you.

319
00:28:05,469 --> 00:28:08,871
- Hello?
- Is this the sheriff's office?

320
00:28:10,421 --> 00:28:11,895
May I speak to him, please?

321
00:28:27,321 --> 00:28:28,321
Thank God.

322
00:28:52,721 --> 00:28:55,121
It may just be a hunch, but...

323
00:28:56,321 --> 00:28:59,971
...I bet the body's inside that van.

324
00:29:03,871 --> 00:29:06,771
Thirty minutes? Believe me, we'll be there.

325
00:29:11,408 --> 00:29:12,997
Thank you, I'm done!

326
00:29:14,899 --> 00:29:18,398
Wait, wait. Can you help me with this?

327
00:29:33,897 --> 00:29:34,792
Are you okay?

328
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:37,921
- Could you...?
- Sure.

329
00:29:49,820 --> 00:29:51,462
Excuse me. Erin?

330
00:29:53,676 --> 00:29:54,571
Excuse me.

331
00:30:06,771 --> 00:30:07,771
Erin?

332
00:30:16,071 --> 00:30:19,221
Excuse me, dear. Could you get the hell out of
the way, son?

333
00:30:23,402 --> 00:30:25,682
We picked her up on the road...

334
00:30:28,423 --> 00:30:29,871
Look at that mess.

335
00:30:41,021 --> 00:30:42,411
Whose is this?

336
00:30:44,471 --> 00:30:47,469
- She had it, sir.
- You don't say?

337
00:30:48,815 --> 00:30:49,971
She had it?

338
00:30:50,773 --> 00:30:51,721
Yes, sir.

339
00:31:01,874 --> 00:31:04,721
All right, calm down. You're not helping.

340
00:31:20,221 --> 00:31:21,621
Hold still, little piggies.

341
00:31:38,645 --> 00:31:39,632
Good Lord.

342
00:32:23,021 --> 00:32:24,321
What the hell was that?

343
00:32:28,249 --> 00:32:29,271
Kemper?

344
00:32:30,921 --> 00:32:31,592
Kemp?

345
00:32:41,528 --> 00:32:44,053
All right, let's wrap her up.

346
00:32:52,602 --> 00:32:54,170
Well, ain't she a pretty one.

347
00:32:55,912 --> 00:32:57,871
I need a hand here, idiot.

348
00:33:00,145 --> 00:33:01,914
I can't do this alone.

349
00:33:03,321 --> 00:33:04,373
I need some help.

350
00:33:08,037 --> 00:33:10,621
I didn't want to get near this. What do I do?

351
00:33:10,676 --> 00:33:13,621
All right, lift her up and turn her toward you.

352
00:33:13,971 --> 00:33:18,321
She won't bite. She's already dead. Grab her and
lift.

353
00:33:18,471 --> 00:33:19,471
Yes, sir.

354
00:33:23,047 --> 00:33:25,312
There you go. That's it.

355
00:33:27,282 --> 00:33:30,171
I'm sure she's very sorry that her damn blood...

356
00:33:30,321 --> 00:33:33,421
...is getting all over your precious arm.

357
00:33:34,421 --> 00:33:35,471
You know...

358
00:33:35,571 --> 00:33:38,371
...when I was a patrolman...

359
00:33:38,471 --> 00:33:41,856
- ...I loved wrapping up these beauties.
- I bet you did.

360
00:33:41,857 --> 00:33:45,221
A cop can get a little sentimental now and then.

361
00:33:49,321 --> 00:33:51,271
Look at that! She's wet down here.

362
00:33:51,321 --> 00:33:53,721
What have you been doing to the body?

363
00:33:53,921 --> 00:33:55,671
Can we just finish this, please?

364
00:34:03,013 --> 00:34:03,971
Kemper?

365
00:34:07,321 --> 00:34:08,073
Kemp?

366
00:34:36,221 --> 00:34:37,271
Is something wrong?

367
00:34:38,171 --> 00:34:39,521
Where is he?

368
00:34:39,818 --> 00:34:40,621
I don't know...

369
00:34:40,721 --> 00:34:42,721
...but he isn't in my house.

370
00:34:43,821 --> 00:34:44,721
Thank you.

371
00:34:53,764 --> 00:34:54,771
Kemper?

372
00:34:59,221 --> 00:34:59,919
Kemp?

373
00:35:05,407 --> 00:35:06,420
Damn it.

374
00:35:07,848 --> 00:35:10,471
All right, boys, there she is.

375
00:35:10,627 --> 00:35:12,621
Let's get her out of here now.

376
00:35:12,737 --> 00:35:16,321
You take her legs, and you grab the top.

377
00:35:17,521 --> 00:35:18,521
Come on, man.

378
00:35:20,542 --> 00:35:21,213
Come on!

379
00:35:25,421 --> 00:35:26,762
Put her in the back seat.

380
00:35:28,144 --> 00:35:30,321
This isn't right.

381
00:35:31,657 --> 00:35:34,121
Don't give me that, young lady.

382
00:35:34,218 --> 00:35:38,571
I've got as much respect for a corpse as for any
of you.

383
00:35:39,917 --> 00:35:40,471
Hey!

384
00:35:40,671 --> 00:35:44,971
Get that goddamn hideous thing out of the back
seat...

385
00:35:45,071 --> 00:35:47,721
...and put her in the trunk.

386
00:35:50,789 --> 00:35:53,721
- Don't break my things.
- Get her legs in.

387
00:36:02,571 --> 00:36:05,063
You gonna be able to find your way out of here?

388
00:36:05,088 --> 00:36:07,476
- Yeah, we'll be fine.
- Very good, then.

389
00:36:09,821 --> 00:36:12,921
To protect and serve. That's what we do.

390
00:36:13,021 --> 00:36:14,621
That's what you did, sir.

391
00:36:22,171 --> 00:36:23,171
Kemp?

392
00:36:31,918 --> 00:36:32,971
Kemper?

393
00:37:24,288 --> 00:37:25,271
Kemper?

394
00:37:35,674 --> 00:37:38,771
Poor Kemper. He'll never get that smell out of
the van.

395
00:37:38,913 --> 00:37:41,171
Think we should try to clean it up for him?

396
00:37:42,072 --> 00:37:43,301
Be my guest.

397
00:37:50,957 --> 00:37:51,770
Are you okay?

398
00:37:52,921 --> 00:37:54,521
This is making me sick.

399
00:37:54,621 --> 00:37:57,141
Well, good news. The sheriff's on his way.

400
00:37:58,473 --> 00:37:59,971
The sheriff's already been here.

401
00:38:02,012 --> 00:38:03,471
He took the body.

402
00:38:04,421 --> 00:38:05,547
Where's Kemper?

403
00:38:06,421 --> 00:38:07,421
Wasn't he with you?

404
00:38:12,684 --> 00:38:15,021
- Kemper?
- What the hell is that?

405
00:38:20,279 --> 00:38:21,471
Kemper?

406
00:38:23,921 --> 00:38:24,605
Kemp?

407
00:38:39,265 --> 00:38:40,571
There's nobody here.

408
00:38:43,872 --> 00:38:45,161
- Kemp?
- What was all that about?

409
00:38:48,159 --> 00:38:49,432
Kemper?

410
00:38:51,147 --> 00:38:52,021
What's that?

411
00:38:53,571 --> 00:38:55,421
Those are somebody's teeth, aren't they?

412
00:38:55,521 --> 00:38:57,321
Pepper, just calm down, okay?

413
00:38:57,541 --> 00:38:59,671
Erin, find your damn boyfriend. It's time to go.

414
00:39:01,366 --> 00:39:02,003
Kemper?

415
00:39:06,868 --> 00:39:07,771
Kemp?

416
00:39:17,221 --> 00:39:18,771
Morgan, what are you doing?

417
00:39:23,630 --> 00:39:24,285
Oh, my God!

418
00:39:27,468 --> 00:39:28,641
Oh, God, help me!

419
00:39:33,773 --> 00:39:35,071
- Idiot.
- That wasn't funny.

420
00:39:41,794 --> 00:39:43,021
What the hell is that?

421
00:39:47,914 --> 00:39:50,221
Isn't that the girl from our van?

422
00:39:51,102 --> 00:39:52,171
It's her.

423
00:39:56,487 --> 00:39:57,471
Is that her family?

424
00:40:00,945 --> 00:40:02,971
What were they doing here?

425
00:40:04,438 --> 00:40:06,471
They were probably looking for the sheriff.

426
00:40:08,043 --> 00:40:09,204
This is really strange.

427
00:40:11,771 --> 00:40:14,196
Let's find Kemper and get the hell out of here.

428
00:40:18,009 --> 00:40:19,321
Where are you going?

429
00:40:19,921 --> 00:40:21,171
To look for him.

430
00:40:22,642 --> 00:40:24,571
Where are the van keys?

431
00:40:28,924 --> 00:40:30,671
Who put you in charge?

432
00:40:32,588 --> 00:40:34,571
If you want to leave, fine...

433
00:40:34,621 --> 00:40:36,771
...but I'm not getting in that van without him.

434
00:40:37,374 --> 00:40:39,208
- Give me the keys.
- No way.

435
00:40:40,876 --> 00:40:42,171
Andy?

436
00:40:42,593 --> 00:40:46,121
I don't know about you guys, but I like my teeth
where they are.

437
00:40:46,989 --> 00:40:48,221
I can't leave him.

438
00:40:48,321 --> 00:40:49,321
Come on.

439
00:40:50,301 --> 00:40:52,071
We'll meet you at the van.

440
00:41:34,321 --> 00:41:35,621
I know Kemp's in there.

441
00:41:35,771 --> 00:41:36,921
Wonderful.

442
00:41:37,174 --> 00:41:38,921
Okay, keep him busy.

443
00:41:48,725 --> 00:41:52,721
Hello, it's me again. Sorry to bother you,
but...

444
00:41:52,821 --> 00:41:56,002
...I couldn't find my boyfriend Kemper, so I
thought...

445
00:41:56,003 --> 00:41:58,121
Weren't you supposed to meet the sheriff?

446
00:42:12,143 --> 00:42:13,021
Kemper?

447
00:42:19,040 --> 00:42:20,921
Kemp, don't fool around.

448
00:42:25,028 --> 00:42:27,121
What a wonderful garden you have.

449
00:42:27,721 --> 00:42:30,174
It's so... wonderful.

450
00:43:29,021 --> 00:43:30,021
Damn it!

451
00:43:34,171 --> 00:43:34,889
Andy?

452
00:43:36,321 --> 00:43:38,343
Hey! You can't come into my house!

453
00:43:39,921 --> 00:43:40,603
Andy?

454
00:43:43,980 --> 00:43:44,972
Are you okay?

455
00:43:46,471 --> 00:43:47,121
Yeah.

456
00:43:52,421 --> 00:43:54,721
What the hell are you doing in my house?

457
00:43:57,321 --> 00:44:00,071
We're just looking for our friend. Then we'll
leave.

458
00:44:00,621 --> 00:44:02,121
You don't give the orders here, boy!

459
00:44:02,271 --> 00:44:03,921
Shut your mouth!

460
00:44:04,421 --> 00:44:05,548
He's crazy.

461
00:44:06,960 --> 00:44:08,771
You fool.

462
00:44:08,871 --> 00:44:11,071
You're so dead, you don't even know it.

463
00:44:14,821 --> 00:44:16,271
Come on, boy.

464
00:44:16,427 --> 00:44:17,621
Bring him!

465
00:44:18,371 --> 00:44:19,371
Bring him.

466
00:44:19,621 --> 00:44:20,921
Bring what?

467
00:44:21,021 --> 00:44:21,821
Bring him!

468
00:44:32,871 --> 00:44:33,521
Shit!

469
00:44:37,771 --> 00:44:39,621
- Come on!
- Andy!

470
00:44:49,421 --> 00:44:51,371
Get out of here! Run!

471
00:45:09,134 --> 00:45:09,921
Shit!

472
00:45:31,171 --> 00:45:33,541
Shit! Oh, God!

473
00:45:57,521 --> 00:45:58,821
Please, stop!

474
00:45:59,171 --> 00:46:01,021
No! Please!

475
00:46:02,021 --> 00:46:03,221
Stop!

476
00:46:04,671 --> 00:46:05,431
Shit!

477
00:46:05,671 --> 00:46:08,171
Erin? Erin?

478
00:46:15,871 --> 00:46:17,960
Kemp's gonna owe us for this.

479
00:46:24,121 --> 00:46:26,021
- What's wrong, Erin?
- Erin, are you okay?

480
00:46:26,121 --> 00:46:27,371
Where's the gun?

481
00:46:28,771 --> 00:46:31,221
- Erin, what's wrong?
- Where's the gun?

482
00:46:31,771 --> 00:46:33,521
The sheriff took it.

483
00:46:34,022 --> 00:46:34,721
Shit!

484
00:46:35,821 --> 00:46:38,637
- Erin, what the hell is going on?
- Shit!

485
00:46:39,058 --> 00:46:40,521
- What?
- What?

486
00:46:43,537 --> 00:46:46,921
- Thank God! Thank God!
- Calm down.

487
00:46:47,321 --> 00:46:51,778
My friend, you have to help him! He's dying, he
was hurt...

488
00:46:52,571 --> 00:46:54,321
Calm down. Take a breath.

489
00:46:54,421 --> 00:46:56,121
There was this guy, he...

490
00:46:56,965 --> 00:46:58,121
Calm down.

491
00:46:59,944 --> 00:47:01,530
- Please.
- What's wrong with your vehicle?

492
00:47:01,602 --> 00:47:05,949
There's nothing wrong with my vehicle. It's my
friend.

493
00:47:07,119 --> 00:47:11,271
Please, help him. I don't know where he is.

494
00:47:11,371 --> 00:47:13,371
Can somebody explain this?

495
00:47:15,879 --> 00:47:16,921
It's not ours.

496
00:47:17,021 --> 00:47:19,021
Are you taking drugs?

497
00:47:20,040 --> 00:47:21,045
- No.
- No.

498
00:47:22,364 --> 00:47:24,071
The van isn't ours.

499
00:47:28,379 --> 00:47:30,271
I smell a bunch of lies.

500
00:47:32,015 --> 00:47:35,121
- No, my friend...
- Get out of the van!

501
00:47:35,621 --> 00:47:36,721
Out!

502
00:47:40,556 --> 00:47:43,171
On the ground! All three of you!

503
00:47:46,013 --> 00:47:47,521
Get down on the ground!

504
00:48:59,821 --> 00:49:00,821
Arizona.

505
00:49:02,389 --> 00:49:03,821
Colorado.

506
00:49:05,432 --> 00:49:07,021
- New York.
- Please...

507
00:49:07,171 --> 00:49:10,821
Help him! He's going to kill him!

508
00:49:11,321 --> 00:49:14,787
Now we're getting somewhere. Who's going to kill
whom?

509
00:49:15,183 --> 00:49:18,003
A man with a goddamn chainsaw!

510
00:49:18,215 --> 00:49:19,821
Get your asses...

511
00:49:19,921 --> 00:49:23,721
...back on the ground until I tell you
otherwise.

512
00:49:27,902 --> 00:49:29,321
You know what I think?

513
00:49:29,421 --> 00:49:32,621
I think your boyfriend shot that little girl.

514
00:49:32,860 --> 00:49:34,871
- And then he ran away.
- He didn't run away.

515
00:49:34,971 --> 00:49:36,851
There's a man with a chainsaw...

516
00:49:39,363 --> 00:49:42,080
- Stop it! Stop it!
- We're gonna die!

517
00:49:42,395 --> 00:49:46,034
You'd better get yourselves under control, or
I'll do it for you.

518
00:49:46,568 --> 00:49:48,158
Why don't you listen to what she's telling you?

519
00:49:49,628 --> 00:49:50,911
Get up.

520
00:49:52,321 --> 00:49:53,671
Stay by the van.

521
00:49:54,416 --> 00:49:57,605
- Stop it! Stop it!
- We're gonna die! We're gonna die!

522
00:49:58,743 --> 00:50:01,971
I want to know exactly what happened inside that
van.

523
00:50:03,321 --> 00:50:06,441
- We already told you what happened.
- Now you're gonna show me.

524
00:50:56,721 --> 00:50:58,621
Is that where she was sitting?

525
00:50:58,971 --> 00:51:01,921
Because the angle doesn't match...

526
00:51:02,021 --> 00:51:03,983
...the blood on the rear windshield.

527
00:51:13,896 --> 00:51:16,321
Maybe she was sitting a little closer to the
middle.

528
00:51:16,821 --> 00:51:20,514
All right, maybe you could move a little more
toward the middle.

529
00:51:22,096 --> 00:51:23,121
But...

530
00:51:25,504 --> 00:51:28,371
What, are you afraid of a little blood?

531
00:51:30,489 --> 00:51:32,085
Move over there!

532
00:51:40,003 --> 00:51:42,771
I don't have much of an imagination...

